course: dictionary
lesson: 13272
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Look at the words around the word first. «The gopher dug a long tunnel under the garden.» Digging a tunnel tells you a gopher is an animal here.
explain: The same word can mean something very different. «Mum sent me as her gopher to fetch milk and bread from the shop.» Nobody here has a tunnel or a tail. A gopher is a person who runs small errands for someone else. This meaning is informal, so you will hear it in chatty speech.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. Does «the animal fetched milk» make sense? No. Does «the errand runner fetched milk» make sense? Yes. That is how you know which meaning fits.
fact: A gopher is a small animal that lives in burrows, which are holes and tunnels dug in the ground.
fact: A pocket gopher has large cheek pouches, which it uses to carry food.
fact: Gophers eat plant roots, and in the USA and Canada they can damage gardens and crops.
fact: In the USA and Canada, the name gopher is also used for ground squirrels.
fact: Informal: a gopher is a person who runs small errands for others, also spelled gofer.
exercise: «The gopher dug a tunnel under the lawn.» What is a gopher in this sentence? | A large bird | A kind of flower | A person who runs errands | *A small burrowing animal
exercise: «Dad said, "Be my gopher and fetch the spanner."» What does gopher mean here? | A tall tree in the garden | A small burrowing animal | A tool for cutting wood | *A person who runs small errands for someone
exercise: «Pocket gophers have big cheek pouches for carrying food.» What are the cheek pouches used for? | Swimming across rivers | *Carrying food | Flying away from danger | Singing loudly
test: The farmers were upset because the gophers had damaged their crops. What did the gophers damage? | The school playground | Rivers and lakes | *Gardens and crops | Roads and bridges
test: Which phrase means a hole dug in the ground by a gopher? | Gopher team | Errand gopher | Gopher mascot | *Gopher hole
exam: In «The Go programming language has a gopher mascot», what does gopher mean? | A person who runs errands | A kind of computer keyboard | A digging rodent with cheek pouches | *A cartoon animal that stands for the language
